==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~50 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,500f</sup>.
*3 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
*3 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Ms. Madonna]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main thing about Ms. Madonna is that she can create wave attacks that will effectively damage your frontlines a lot. So the use of small 75¢ meatshields are ineffective, instead opting for tankier ones are better considering it can both tank the waves and the constant fists of Shadow Boxer Ks. [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] is quite a good choice.

Use [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] to outrange any Kang Roos, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for Shadow Boxer K, and [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Skelecat]] For Zang Roos.Then use [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] to tank. If Ms. Madonna dies, don't forget to spawn some meatshields, like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and the [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Version]].

